vaporOS nuttx-apps patch: readline-completer-hook

Problem:   NuttX readline's Tab completion only completes *builtin app names*
           for the whole line. A shell needs per-word completion: commands at
           command position, file names everywhere else.
Evidence:  `ls /fl<Tab>` did nothing useful; `ec<Tab>` could complete only apps.
Fix:       readline_completer(fn) registers an application hook
           fn(line, len, insert_buf, insert_len, list_cb, ctx). Readline calls it on
           Tab, inserts what it returns, and prints the candidate list.
           The list, prompt and line are gathered and written with ONE write():
           the old byte-at-a-time output of a list was what first exposed the
           USB console wedge (see nuttx/cdcacm-tx-ring-race.patch).
           vaporshell registers vs_complete() (vaporshell/complete.c).
Upstream:  MAYBE. A completion callback is a generally useful readline feature, but
           this is a quick hook, not a designed API (no cursor-in-middle support,
           one global hook). Would need a cleaner interface to be accepted.
Note:      readline_completer() is a process-global hook: a program that reads
           lines while vaporshell's hook is installed (vlua's REPL) must clear it
           with readline_completer(NULL).

diff --git a/include/system/readline.h b/include/system/readline.h
index 5ab963879..390230c16 100644
--- a/include/system/readline.h
+++ b/include/system/readline.h
@@ -144,6 +144,34 @@ FAR const struct extmatch_vtable_s *
   readline_extmatch(FAR const struct extmatch_vtable_s *vtbl);
 #endif
 
+/****************************************************************************
+ * Name: readline_completer
+ *
+ *   vaporOS addition. Registers a callback that replaces the built-in
+ *   builtin-name-only tab completion with application-defined completion
+ *   (per-word, paths, ...).
+ *
+ *   The callback receives the text before the cursor (line[0..len)) and
+ *   must write the text to insert at the cursor (the common prefix of all
+ *   candidates, minus what was already typed) into ins[0..inslen). It
+ *   returns the number of candidates; when that is more than one it must
+ *   also call list() once per candidate so readline can display them.
+ *
+ * Returned values:
+ *   The previously registered completer.
+ *
+ ****************************************************************************/
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_READLINE_TABCOMPLETION
+typedef CODE void (*readline_list_f)(FAR void *ctx, FAR const char *name);
+typedef CODE int (*readline_completer_f)(FAR const char *line, int len,
+                                         FAR char *ins, int inslen,
+                                         readline_list_f list,
+                                         FAR void *ctx);
+
+readline_completer_f readline_completer(readline_completer_f fn);
+#endif
+
 /****************************************************************************
  * Name: readline_fd
  *
